 B. Timed-Elastic-Band (TEB) Optimization Problem
This section introduces the TEB optimization formulation.
The overall objective is to steer the car-like robot from a
start ss to a desired goal configuration sf in minimum time.
The underlying optimization problem is defined in terms
of a finite-dimensional parameter vector composed of the
discretized sequence of n robot configurations (sk)k=1,2,...,n
